text:
Maya (Support): FYI escalated from VIP customer (ticket #C-4982). They report duplicate charges after a sequence of 429s + 502s on the /v1/payments endpoint. Browser app using JS SDK v1.2.3. Need quick triage and short-term mitigation. https://support.example/t/C-4982 :eyes:
Jordan (SRE): Can you paste the timeline + request IDs? First-pass guess: client retry storm + no idempotency key. We need to see response headers (Retry-After, X-RateLimit-*) and client retry config.
Maya (Support): Customer attached logs — root request id pmt_01G8E5X0 and sample sequence: 429 (Retry-After: 1), then 502 gateway, then client retried 3 times within ~800ms intervals and we see 2 successful charge events.
billing-bot: AUDIT: billing spike detected for acct_777 (2 duplicative charges flagged).
Kevin (SDK): Quick note — JS SDK v1.2.3 default retries=2, linear backoff 500ms (we changed to expo in v1.3). Also there was a known bug in v1.2.3 where Retry-After from fetch polyfill was ignored in browsers. Could explain aggressive retries.
Samir (Payments): Confirming server requires Idempotency-Key for safe retrying. Without it, each POST can create a new charge. We should treat this as customer-side missing header + old SDK behavior.
Maya (Support): Customer says they set idempotency in some flows but not consistently (mobile uses it, web didn't). They were on v1.2.3 in prod.
Jordan (SRE): Immediate mitigation suggestions: 1) recommend customer to set Idempotency-Key for every payment request; 2) instruct to upgrade SDK to v1.3+ or apply canary patch we provide; 3) server: ensure we respect Idempotency-Key and return consistent 409/200 semantics for duplicates; 4) verify our rate-limit headers include Retry-After and X-RateLimit-Reset on this route.
Kevin (SDK): Patch plan: I'll cut a hotfix branch that (a) respects Retry-After on browser fetch, (b) changes default retry strategy to exponential backoff with full jitter, and (c) sets retries=3 with max backoff 5s. Example snippet for recommended client config (send to customer):

```
// recommended pattern for browser SDK
const client = new RedwoodClient({
  retry: {
    attempts: 3,
    backoff: (attempt) => {
      // full jitter expo: min(1000*2**attempt, 5000) * random()
      return Math.min(1000 * Math.pow(2, attempt), 5000) * Math.random();
    },
    respectRetryAfter: true
  }
});
await client.post('/v1/payments', { body }, { headers: { 'Idempotency-Key': uuidv4() } });
```

Kevin (SDK): I'll tag a canary release and DM Maya the build. :thumbsup:
Samir (Payments): Longer term: add server-side guard rails: if no Idempotency-Key present on payments route, return a warning header and rate-limit more aggressively; also add duplicate-detection alerts that automatically create a make-right ticket when two charge events share near identical payloads within a short window.
Jordan (SRE): Also check our proxy config — there's a brief window where upstream 502s cascade into client retries. We can tune the proxy retry policy to avoid double-retries (proxy should not auto-retry mutating POSTs).
Maya (Support): Repro steps for eng/QA from customer: 1) Use browser SDK v1.2.3, 2) send payment POST without Idempotency-Key, 3) simulate 429 then 502, 4) observe multiple successful charges. Attaching curl example and request ids in ticket.
Kevin (SDK): Request from me: can we get a sample raw request/response pair (headers + bodies) for pmt_01G8E5X0? I'll run it against canary to confirm fix.
Samir (Payments): I'll add logging to surface Idempotency-Key presence/duplicate matches for last 72h and backfill duplicates for this account.
Maya (Support): Short-term customer-facing guidance I'll send: 1) rotate to SDK v1.3+ (or apply hotfix), 2) set Idempotency-Key for every unique payment intent, 3) implement exponential backoff with jitter and respect Retry-After, 4) if duplicates persist, send request ids for manual refund/rollback.
Jordan (SRE): Postmortem action items: (a) ensure proxy doesn't retry POSTs silently; (b) add test to SDK pipeline to validate Retry-After handling in browser; (c) add a monitoring alert when we see >1 charge event per request-id pattern.
Kevin (SDK): I'll post the canary link by EOD and include backoff example for mobile/web.
Maya (Support): Thanks everyone — assigning owners: Kevin (SDK hotfix), Samir (payments guardrails + duplicates), Jordan (proxy config + monitoring), Maya will coordinate customer comms. I'll update ticket C-4982 after we confirm canary. :white_check_mark:
